        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9c2df8dc-a47a-5251-9d02-4d784c480ff5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Documents: Declaration to the Seven, Balfour Declaration, Sykes-Picot Agreement\n- People: Sir Henry McMahon\n- Organizations: British government, Party of Syrian Unity, Bolsheviks\n- Places: Cairo, Syria, Palestine\n- Topics: World War I, Zionism, Ottoman Empire\n\nFacts:\n- The Balfour Declaration was a public statement issued by the British government during World War I supporting the establishment of a national home for the Jewish people in Palestine, which was then an Ottoman region with a minority Jewish population.\n- The Sykes-Picot Agreement was a secret agreement between Britain and France dated May 1916.\n- The Bolsheviks published the secret Sykes-Picot Agreement on November 23, 1917.\n- The Party of Syrian Unity was newly formed in the wake of the Balfour Declaration and the November 23, 1917 Bolshevik publication of the Sykes-Picot Agreement.\n- Seven Syrian notables in Cairo who belonged to the Party of Syrian Unity anonymously issued a memorandum.\n- The Declaration to the Seven was written by British diplomat Sir Henry McMahon and released on June 16, 1918 in response to the memorandum from the seven Syrian notables in Cairo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "89ac73b6-6b3b-543d-b7e2-c6b82a211b29",
        "text": "Page: Declaration to the Seven. Sentence: The Declaration to the Seven was a document written by the British diplomat Sir Henry McMahon and released on June 16, 1918 in response to a memorandum issued anonymously by seven Syrian notables in Cairo who were members of the newly formed Party of Syrian Unity, established in the wake of the Balfour Declaration and the November 23, 1917 publication by the Bolsheviks of the secret May 1916 Sykes-Picot Agreement between Britain and France.\nPage: Balfour Declaration. Sentence: The Balfour Declaration was a public statement issued by the British government during World War I announcing support for the establishment of a \"national home for the Jewish people\" in Palestine, then an Ottoman region with a minority Jewish population.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
